'''Rui''' (累, ''Rui'') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in the [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 15.1 Update#Version 15.1.1 Update|Version 15.1.1]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Rui
|image = E 761.png
|first appearance = [[Swarm of Spiders]]
|money drop = 2,000¢ - 7,900¢
}}

==Enemy==
Rui can come off as a menacing foe, boasting a strong 100,000 health, 450 range and a 50% chance to [[Slow]] [[Cat Units]], but his damage isn't that high even at his highest magnification. The strongest you'll ever see Rui is at 450% at {{1c}} and 675% at {{2c}}. His decently average time between attacks allows you to get a couple of hits on him with fast melee units, and makes him vulnerable to any [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless Cats]] that have status effects such as [[Freeze]], [[Weaken]], [[Slow]], etc.

==Strategy==
Rui outranges many standard backline attackers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]], etc. The best way to take him down is to use rushers like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to deal high damage in between attack cycles. However, [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]], [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Heavy]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Dark Emperor Catdam]] are some notable exceptions that outrange Rui, and can be used to provide consistent chip damage and crowd-control against him.

Midgame players can use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to rush him down for timed rewards, or [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]] for their phenomenal support through Freeze.

